.TH WALLPAPERFISH 1
.SH NAME
wallpaperfish \- an aquarium for a desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/wallpaperfish
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I WallPaperFish
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/WallPaperFish.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Sixteen critters of three kinds, each a four-frame cycle whose middle
frame is shared going out and coming back.  Positions are kept in fixed
point, which is why a critter that swims off one edge reappears at the
other for nothing, and one swimming left is drawn mirrored about a
vertical line through itself rather than from a second set of sprites.
The water is one diagonal every twenty pixels with an offset that is a
triangle wave of the clock, so the whole rack slides.
.PP
The original replaces the desktop's own paint routine and has to be
included into the system task so its code outlives the program \- "Would
crash when code mem was freed."  An Inferno client cannot paint
.IR wm (1)'s
background, so this draws in its own window.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/wallpaperfish.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
